          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
            is sometimes called its “tautological line bundle”. (For more background see also at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In the following, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-algebra"} star
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-field"} skew-field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi StarSkewFields
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k \,\in\, StarSkewFields
                  \\,.
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+topology"} differential topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            being one of the three
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+normed+division+algebras"} real normed division algebras
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"}> real numbers
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            or
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k \,\in\, \big\{ \mathbb{R}, \mathbb{C}, \mathbb{H}\big\}
          %p
            equipped with their canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+conjugation"} conjugation
            operations.
          %p
            The relevance of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            here is the reason to insist on the generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-fields"} skew-fields
            and hence of some pedantry about order of products and distinction of left/right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
            in the following. (For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            the notion of tautological lines should make some sense over the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+projective+space"} octonionic projective space
            but not beyond.)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
          %h3#BareDefinition Tautological line bundle and blow-up
          %p
            The
            %em
